# Ship after green

This user does not want to be asked to commit or push.

After the work is done:

1. Run `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build`.
2. If either fails, fix it and re-run both. Do not commit.
3. If both pass and there are real changes, commit (HEREDOC, skip `.env`/secrets) and `git push -u origin HEAD`.
4. Do not ask. Do not wait. Say the commit hash when done.

A Cursor stop hook will nudge you if you finish with a green build and a dirty tree. Obey it.
